; DOMAIN: kummer-sequence [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-25]
; Claim: For an elliptic curve E/Q and integer n>=2, multiplication-by-n gives a short exact sequence of Galois modules 0->E[n]->E(Qbar)->E(Qbar)->0; taking G_Q-cohomology yields the Kummer sequence 0->E(Q)/nE(Q)->H^1(G_Q,E[n])->H^1(G_Q,E)[n]->0. The connecting (Kummer) map delta: E(Q)/nE(Q) -> H^1(G_Q,E[n]) sends P to the cocycle sigma |-> sigma(Q)-Q where nQ=P. Imposing local conditions (image of the local Kummer map at every place v) cuts out the n-Selmer group; the quotient measures Sha[n], giving 0->E(Q)/nE(Q)->Sel_n(E/Q)->Sha(E/Q)[n]->0. This is the cohomological engine of descent and the finiteness of E(Q)/nE(Q) (weak Mordell-Weil). Bridge: genesis_mordell_weil (weak MW finiteness of E(Q)/nE(Q) via this injection) + genesis_selmer_group (local conditions on the Kummer image define Sel_n) + genesis_galois_representation (E[n] as the G_Q-module whose H^1 hosts the sequence).
(= (kummer-sequence $E $n) (exact-sequence (div (rational-points $E) (mult $n (rational-points $E))) (H1 (galois-group Q) (torsion-mod $E $n)) (torsion (H1 (galois-group Q) $E) $n)))
(= (kummer-map $E $n $P) (cocycle (lambda $sigma (sub (act $sigma (n-division-point $E $n $P)) (n-division-point $E $n $P)))))
(= (selmer-from-kummer $E $n) (fiber-product (kummer-map $E $n) (local-image $E $n)))
(= (descent-ses $E $n) (exact-sequence (div (rational-points $E) (mult $n (rational-points $E))) (selmer-group $E $n) (torsion (sha-group $E) $n)))